<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ross, Scotland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ross is a region of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scottish-highlands">Highlands of Scotland</a> stretching from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moray-firth">Moray Firth</a> to the west coast. It became an earldom in the early 13th century, and the claim of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donald-lord-of-the-isles">Donald, Lord of the Isles</a>, to the earldom led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-harlaw">Battle of Harlaw</a> in 1411. The Lords of the Isles held the earldom from 1437 until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-islay-earl-of-ross">John of Islay</a> forfeited it to the crown in 1475. It later formed the county of Ross and Cromarty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ross-scotland.jpg" alt="Ross, Scotland" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benson85 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ross_(district).PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
